nodes.statement:
We say that a nilspace $\mathrm{X}$ is an \textsc{lch}\emph{ nilspace} if $\mathrm{X}$ is a locally-compact Haursdorff second-countable topological space such that the following property holds for every integer $n\geq 0$:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The cube set $\mathrm{C}^n(\mathrm{X})$ is closed in the product topology on $\mathrm{X}^{\llbracket n\rrbracket}$.
    \item The coordinate projection $p^{\llbracket n\rrbracket}:\mathrm{C}^n(\mathrm{X})\rightarrow \mathrm{Cor}^n(\mathrm{X})$ is an open map.
\end{enumerate}

Let $n$ be a non-negative integer, and let  $\binom{\cdot}{n}$ denote the map $\mathbb{Z}\rightarrow \mathbb{Z}$ sending $x$ to the binomial coefficient $\binom{x}{n}$. Then for every $i\ge 1$ the map $\binom{\cdot}{n}$ is a morphism $\mathcal{D}_i(\mathbb{Z})\rightarrow \mathcal{D}_{ni}(\mathbb{Z})$.

Let $(A_i)_{i=1}^k$ be a sequence of abelian groups, and let $\mathrm{X}$ be the product nilspace $\prod_{i=1}^k\mathcal{D}_i(A_i)$. Then for each $s\in [k]$ we have
\begin{equation}
\Theta_s(\mathrm{X}) = \prod_{i=1}^k \hom\left(\prod_{j=1}^{i-s} \mathcal{D}_j(A_j),\mathcal{D}_{i-s}(A_i)\right),
\end{equation}

where the action of an element $(0,\ldots,0,T_s,T_{s+1},\ldots,T_k)$ in this product, as a translation $\alpha\in \Theta_s(\mathrm{X})$, is defined by $\alpha(x)=(x_1,\ldots,x_k)+(0,\ldots,0,T_s,T_{s+1}(x_1),\ldots,T_k(x_1,\ldots,x_{k-s}))$.
